{
  "code": "MATSC-BS",
  "reviewed": "2026-10-23",
  "summary": "The audit checks the School of Engineering requirements (39 combined units of Math and Science, at least 16 of them Science, Technology in Society, and 7 units of Engineering Fundamentals), the 25 units of Materials Science Fundamentals, four depth lab courses for 15 units, one focus area of three courses for 9 units including a MATSCI course, WIM and a capstone track. Every course must be letter graded when the instructor offers a letter grade, with a C or better. Checked by hand: the 2.7 combined GPA, a self-defined focus area, a petitioned non-MatSci lab course, up to six units of MATSCI 150 an honors student counts toward the focus area (they still count for honors, but not as the focus area's MATSCI course), and AP credit toward the science units. Honors is optional.",
  "nodes": {
